  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following is true?<br />\r(i) If <math><mi>p</mi></math> is a statement then <math><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi></math> is not a statement<br />\r(ii) If <math><mi>p</mi></math> is a statement then <math><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi></math> is also a statement<br />\r(iii) Negation of \"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>x</mi></math> is a positive real number\" is, \"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is a negative real number\"",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KWxhf",
      "text": "Only (ii)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "UmaVI",
      "text": "Only (i)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Nb5Sf",
      "text": "(i) and (iii)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ogAIj",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As per definition of statement,negation of a statement is also a statement<br />Negation of <math><mi>p</mi></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is not a positive real number.",
